<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Omni Media headline year EPS up 12 percent.</title>
<headline>Omni Media headline year EPS up 12 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		256	   vs 229</p>
<p>    - attrib		  454	   vs 135</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  62	   vs  54</p>
<p>    Attrib income	  273.94	 vs  79.85</p>
<p>    Headline income	154.84	 vs 135.35</p>
<p>    Exceptional gain	119.09	vs  55.49 charge</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   214.11	vs 176.28</p>
<p>    Tax			  58.00	vs  62.14</p>
<p>    Interest received	 5.34	vs   1.94</p>
<p>    Investment income	27.72	vs  23.96</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  141.98	vs  26.84</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2,215.81    vs 1,989.62</p>
<p>Div payable August 15</p>
<p>on register July 25</p>
<p>Full name: Omni Media Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Exceptionals reflect profit on sale of investments.</p>
<p>The publishing, broadcasting and retail group said it was well poised to show positive earnings growth for the coming year, given an improvement in business confidence.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
